---
title: Sync & data
description: How Muse boards persist to your NeoWorks account and stay in sync across devices.
---

Muse has no database of its own. Boards, objects, and folders are written straight to your
NeoWorks account through the platform data plane, so the same content is available on every
device you sign in from.

## Two kinds of data

Muse splits what it stores the same way the platform does:

- **Structured** — board layout, object positions, folders. Queryable, so Muse can load only
  the board you open. Lives in the [OpenSchema layer](/docs/neoworks/openschema).
- **Media** — images and other uploaded blobs. [Encrypted end-to-end](/docs/neoworks/storage)
  with keys only you hold; Muse uploads and fetches them through the NeoWorks Vault.

## Authentication

Muse signs in with the standard NeoWorks [OAuth](/docs/neoworks/oauth) flow and requests scopes
for the board schemas plus media storage. Tokens are short-lived and refreshed transparently.

## Real-time

Edits publish to the same real-time event stream the platform uses, so a board open on two
devices converges without a manual refresh.
